-- title:
--   Supports of consecutive ideal sheaves on the resolution meet
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and $t \in W$ an element that is not a unit, and let $e$ be a natural number. Write $\mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\,W\,t$ for the quotient $W[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1 - t)$ (the multivariate polynomial ring in two variables modulo the principal ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - C(t)$), and let `Resolution t e` be the scheme obtained as the colimit of the diagram `glueDiagram t e` over the index category `GlueIndex e`, with chart morphisms $\iota_i =$ `ι t e i` for $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,e$ from the chart scheme into it. Suppose given a family $F : \mathrm{Fin}(e+1) \to$ `(Resolution t e).IdealSheafData` of ideal sheaf data on the resolution, satisfying the chart table: for every chart index $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,e$ and every $k \in \mathrm{Fin}(e+1)$, the pullback `(F k).comap (ι t e i)` is the ideal sheaf `ofIdealTop` attached to the transport, along the inverse of `Scheme.ΓSpecIso` for `CommRingCat.of (CrossingQuotient W t)`, of the ideal which is the span of $\{V t\}$ if $k = i$, the span of $\{U t\}$ if $k = i+1$, and the unit ideal otherwise. Then for every natural number $k < e$ there exists a point $z$ of `Resolution t e` lying both in the support of $F_k$ and in the support of $F_{k+1}$.
--
--   This is the statement that two consecutive members of the chart-table family of ideal sheaves on the toric resolution of $uv = t^e$ have intersecting supports, i.e. that the corresponding components of the special fibre meet; the non-unit hypothesis on $t$ is what makes the supports non-empty at all. It is used in the assembly of the special fibre package attached to the chart table, `specialFibrePackage_of_chartTable`, where the chain of $e+1$ components is shown to be connected.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPolynomial_CrossingQuotient_Resolution_exists_mem_support_and_mem_support_succ.lean

